# hello

Created with `cfgx init`. Settings are declared in
[internal/settings/schema](internal/settings/schema/schema.go); the code that
reads them, the example config and [docs/CONFIG.md](docs/CONFIG.md) are
generated from it.

```sh
go build .
./hello serve                  # listens on localhost:8080
./hello serve --server-addr :9090
./hello config explain         # every setting, its value and where it came from
```

## Adding a setting

1. Declare it in `internal/settings/schema/schema.go`, for example
   `dsl.Int("max_body", "Largest request body, in bytes").Default(1 << 20)`
   in the `Server` group.
2. Run `go generate ./...`.
3. Read it with the generated getter, `s.ServerMaxBody()`.

It can then be set with `--server-max-body`, `HELLO_SERVER_MAX_BODY`
or `server.max_body` in `hello.yaml` (see `hello.example.yaml`).
